sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant S as PrivateStore<br/>(0700 dir, atomic snapshots)
  participant J as httpjet<br/>acme manager
  participant CA as ACME CA<br/>(RFC 8555)
  participant R as TLS resolvers<br/>TCP · QUIC · kTLS
  J->>S: persist account key (before registration)
  J->>CA: newAccount / newOrder (bounded HTTP: 5 s connect, 10 s request, 1 MiB)
  J->>S: persist certificate key + CSR (before finalize)
  CA-->>J: authorization → http-01 token
  J->>J: register token in ChallengeRegistry (≤128 live, TTL ≤15 min)
  CA->>J: GET http://host/.well-known/acme-challenge/<token> (port 80, plaintext only)
  J-->>CA: key authorization (Cache-Control: no-store — no rewrite, cache, auth or backend involved)
  J->>CA: finalize → poll (120 s attempt deadline, backoff + Retry-After)
  CA-->>J: certificate chain
  J->>J: validate chain, validity, exact SAN set, key match
  J->>S: commit cert + key + order state in ONE snapshot
  J->>R: publish immutable CertifiedKey overlay (exact-SNI)
  Note over J,R: renewal scheduled with 1/3 of remaining lifetime in reserve (+ jitter)
